{"id":"f900d02215c06646","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-multitape-dtm-language-simulation.md","title":"Single-Tape and Multitape Equivalence","display":"thm-multitape-turing-equivalence — Single-Tape and Multitape Equivalence","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-multitape-dtm-language-simulation","aliases":["73-thm-multitape-dtm-language-simulation","73-thm-multitape-turing-equivalence"],"display":"thm-multitape-turing-equivalence — Single-Tape and Multitape Equivalence","depends_on":["[[73-df-multitape-dtm-semantics]]","[[73-df-dtm-language-semantics]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Automata Theory, Languages and Computation (Hopcroft, Ullman)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-multitape-dtm-language-simulation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-multitape-dtm-language-simulation</span><span>73-thm-multitape-turing-equivalence</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-multitape-turing-equivalence — Single-Tape and Multitape Equivalence"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"9fa7db79fea5f29a\" href=\"?note=9fa7db79fea5f29a\" title=\"73-df-multitape-dtm-semantics\">73-df-multitape-dtm-semantics</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"888d8ab66ec7efca\" href=\"?note=888d8ab66ec7efca\" title=\"73-df-dtm-language-semantics\">73-df-dtm-language-semantics</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbf 2=\\{0,1\\}\">\\(\\mathbf 2=\\{0,1\\}\\)</span> (binary alphabet)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{DTM}_{\\mathbf 2}\">\\(\\mathsf{DTM}_{\\mathbf 2}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{MDTM}_{\\mathbf 2}\">\\(\\operatorname{MDTM}_{\\mathbf 2}\\)</span> (single-tape and multitape deterministic machines)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L(\\cdot)\">\\(L(\\cdot)\\)</span> (the corresponding accepted-language maps)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}multitape\\text{-}turing\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\left[\n\\exists M\\;(\\operatorname{MDTM}_{\\mathbf 2}(M)\\land L=L(M))\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists S\\in\\mathsf{DTM}_{\\mathbf 2}\\;(L=L(S))\n\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}multitape\\text{-}turing\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\left[\n\\exists M\\;(\\operatorname{MDTM}_{\\mathbf 2}(M)\\land L=L(M))\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists S\\in\\mathsf{DTM}_{\\mathbf 2}\\;(L=L(S))\n\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A single-tape machine is the <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k=1\">\\(k=1\\)</span> case. Conversely, one tape stores all <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span> tapes in delimited tracks and sweeps across them to simulate one multitape step.</li>\n<li>Breadth and delimiters are finite for each simulated configuration, so the simulation preserves acceptance, rejection, and divergence; its standard time overhead is at most quadratic.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-multitape-dtm-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"9fa7db79fea5f29a","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-multitape-dtm-semantics]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-dtm-language-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"888d8ab66ec7efca","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-dtm-language-semantics]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathbf 2=\\{0,1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathsf{DTM}_{\\mathbf 2}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{MDTM}_{\\mathbf 2}","display":false},{"tex":"L(\\cdot)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}multitape\\text{-}turing\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\left[\n\\exists M\\;(\\operatorname{MDTM}_{\\mathbf 2}(M)\\land L=L(M))\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists S\\in\\mathsf{DTM}_{\\mathbf 2}\\;(L=L(S))\n\\right]","display":true},{"tex":"k=1","display":false},{"tex":"k","display":false}],"bytes":1346,"backlinks":[{"id":"31034767f7505eb4","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""}],"outgoing":["9fa7db79fea5f29a","888d8ab66ec7efca"]}